# SEO Engine — example requests.
#
# For editors with an HTTP client (VS Code REST Client, JetBrains .http). Run
# the login block first, copy the access_token into @token, then the rest.
# Nothing here is authoritative — /api/v1/openapi.json is — but these are the
# calls you reach for first.

@base = http://localhost:8000/api/v1
@token = PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN_HERE

### Liveness (no auth)
GET {{base}}/../healthz

### Readiness — checks the database (no auth)
GET {{base}}/../readyz

### Register a new account + organisation
POST {{base}}/auth/register
content-type: application/json

{
  "email": "you@example.com",
  "password": "a-strong-password-123",
  "name": "You",
  "organisation_name": "Your Org"
}

### Log in
POST {{base}}/auth/login
content-type: application/json

{ "email": "you@example.com", "password": "a-strong-password-123" }

### Who am I (permissions included)
GET {{base}}/auth/me
authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a brand
POST {{base}}/brands
authorization: Bearer {{token}}
content-type: application/json

{ "name": "Acme Diagnostics", "industry": "diagnostics", "risk_category": "health" }

### List brands (paginated; meta.total is the tenant's count)
GET {{base}}/brands
authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Add a service to a brand
POST {{base}}/brands/BRAND_ID/services
authorization: Bearer {{token}}
content-type: application/json

{ "name": "DNA testing", "keywords": ["dna testing", "paternity test"], "revenue_weight": 2.0 }

### Connect Search Console (development-adapter mode without credentials)
POST {{base}}/brands/BRAND_ID/integrations
authorization: Bearer {{token}}
content-type: application/json

{ "provider": "google_search_console" }

### Add a website
POST {{base}}/brands/BRAND_ID/websites
authorization: Bearer {{token}}
content-type: application/json

{ "url": "https://acme.example" }

### Start a technical audit (202; poll the crawls / runs endpoints)
POST {{base}}/websites/WEBSITE_ID/audit
authorization: Bearer {{token}}
content-type: application/json

{ "max_pages": 50, "max_depth": 3 }

### Plan a mission
POST {{base}}/brands/BRAND_ID/missions
authorization: Bearer {{token}}
content-type: application/json

{ "objective": "Increase qualified organic leads", "website_id": "WEBSITE_ID" }

### Run a mission (202)
POST {{base}}/missions/MISSION_ID/run
authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Read a mission: status, baseline, task graph, progress, metrics
GET {{base}}/missions/MISSION_ID
authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Recommendations (each cites evidence; health brands require approval)
GET {{base}}/brands/BRAND_ID/recommendations
authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Approve a recommendation
POST {{base}}/recommendations/RECOMMENDATION_ID/approve
authorization: Bearer {{token}}
content-type: application/json

{ "note": "Approved for drafting" }

### The agent registry and their declared contracts
GET {{base}}/agents
authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Agent runs for a mission (the observable record)
GET {{base}}/agents/runs?mission_id=MISSION_ID
authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Semantic memory search (this tenant only)
GET {{base}}/memory/search?q=brand%20profile&brand_id=BRAND_ID
authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The audit log (requires audit.read)
GET {{base}}/audit
authorization: Bearer {{token}}
